# Every checked-in file must arrive byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Provenance pins SHA-256 hashes of repository files, of preserved upstream
# datasets, and of the scanner's own runtime closure. A platform that rewrites
# line endings on checkout therefore breaks those hashes rather than merely
# changing whitespace: a Windows runner with the default core.autocrlf produced
# UnicodeData-15.1.0.txt as eb82eed7... instead of the pinned 2fc713e6..., and
# the generated case-fold verification refused it. The same translation would
# give the scanner runtime closure a different composite digest on Windows than
# on Linux, so receipts would not be reproducible across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Preserved upstream material is never translated at all. Its bytes are the
# artifact being attested, not a convenience for an editor.
schemas/third-party-data/** -text
schemas/third-party-licenses/** -text
